    "senderName": "NWS Los Angeles/Oxnard CA",
    "headline": "Flood Advisory issued October 22 at 9:11AM PDT until October 22 at 11:00AM PDT by NWS Los Angeles/Oxnard CA",
    "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Western Los Angeles County in southwestern California...\nNorthern Ventura County in southwestern California...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1100 AM PDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas. Rock\nslides and mud slides possible.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 910 AM PDT, Doppler radar indicated isolated areas of locally\nheavy rain due to showers and thunderstorms. Minor flooding is\nongoing or expected to begin shortly in the advisory area. Rock\nand mud slides possible.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMalibu, Acton, Ojai, Chatsworth, Northridge, Woodland Hills,\nSanta Clarita, Agoura Hills, Van Nuys, Encino, North Hollywood,\nSanta Monica, Beverly Hills, Universal City, Burbank, Hollywood\nand Venice.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
    "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.",
    "response": "Avoid",
